   28   * ## Error Handling on GET /user
   29   *
   30   * - 4XX errors (400, 401, 403, 404): Token is invalid → logout, clear token
   31   * - 5XX errors (500, 503) or network errors: Server is down → keep token, auto-retry
   32   *
   33   * The distinction matters: a 401 means "your token is bad" (clear it), while a 500
   34   * means "server is broken" (keep the token, it might work when server recovers).
   35   *
   36   * ## Auto-Retry
   37   *
   38   * When in 'unavailable' state, the service automatically retries with exponential
   39   * backoff: 2s → 4s → 8s → 16s → 16s → ... (capped at 16s, retries indefinitely).
   40   * The UI shows "Connecting..." while retrying. User can also just reload the page.
   41   *
